  "principles": [
    "Base consultation facts and optional candidate semantics remain separate through PB-06.",
    "Raw optional_message is visible only to deterministic Safety, PB-01C, PB-04, and PB-06.",
    "Candidate semantic Safety reaches PB-02 through a separate nullable key.",
    "PB-04, PB-05, and PB-06 receive Application-owned CandidateEnvelope explicitly.",
    "PB-04 and PB-06 treat raw optional_message as inert untrusted user data, never as an instruction.",
    "No downstream payload contains a merged Structured Intake that can relabel candidate content as an observed consultation fact.",
    "Application code owns presence, provenance, IDs, sequence, nullability, canonical Base fields, policy, eligibility, and aggregate Safety."
  ],
